  "description": "#6051 — an undo refuses to revive a tag name another live tag of its space holds, as a rename does, and changes nothing. The ops make a space (`C1`) and four tags in it, `work` (C2), `spare` (C3), `notes` (C4) and `extra` (C5), all before any delete so every create lands on a dense root. C2 is trashed and C3 renamed to `work`: undoing the delete (O16) would put two live `work` tags in the space, so it is refused with `DuplicatePageTitle`, C2 stays in the trash and no op is appended. C4 is renamed to `job` (O18) and C5 takes `notes`: undoing O18 is refused the same way, so C4 keeps `job`. Reverting or undoing O19 and O16 together is refused whole, so C5 keeps `notes` though O19 alone reverts cleanly. Once C3 is trashed `work` is free, and the same undo of O16 restores C2.",
